fault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwE2CNACELwBSFXyq4qpAygIARUAAIhCGAFwAcABBvABAfgB_gSAAuACigIMCAAQARhlIGEoWTAP&rs=AOn4CLB6fWsKfKfiIud-ygi0G4l_CS4Jfw", "height": 188, "width": 336, "preference": -7, "id": "39", "resolution": "336x188"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/8p47AbBSOI8/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwE9CNACELwBSFryq4qpAy8IARUAAAAAGAElAADIQj0AgKJDeAHwAQH4Af4EgALgAooCDAgAEAEYZSBhKFkwDw==&rs=AOn4CLAvImqtHN7hb9uO1P_d3DJNgp0yLw", "height": 188, "width": 336, "preference": -7, "id": "40", "resolution": "336x188"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/8p47AbBSOI8/hqdefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEmCOADEOgC8quKqQMa8AEB-AH-BIAC4AKKAgwIABABGGUgYShZMA8=&rs=AOn4CLB9aCvUp6u41M-KhLry2GrQAlNk5A", "height": 360, "width": 480, "preference": -7, "id": "41", "resolution": "480x360"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/8p47AbBSOI8/hqdefault.webp", "preference": -6, "id": "42"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/8p47AbBSOI8/sddefault.jpg", "preference": -5, "id": "43"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/8p47AbBSOI8/sddefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEmCIAFEOAD8quKqQMa8AEB-AH-BIAC4AKKAgwIABABGGUgYShZMA8=&rs=AOn4CLAayw7UOOMcLGnZ62RK_G-hTRs-8g", "height": 480, "width": 640, "preference": -5, "id": "44", "resolution": "640x480"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/8p47AbBSOI8/sddefault.webp", "preference": -4, "id": "45"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/8p47AbBSOI8/hq720.jpg", "preference": -3, "id": "46"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/8p47AbBSOI8/hq720.webp", "preference": -2, "id": "47"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/8p47AbBSOI8/maxresdefault.jpg", "preference": -1, "id": "48"}, {"url": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi_webp/8p47AbBSOI8/maxresdefault.webp", "preference": 0, "id": "49"}], "thumbnail": "https://i.ytimg.com/vi/8p47AbBSOI8/sddefault.jpg?sqp=-oaymwEmCIAFEOAD8quKqQMa8AEB-AH-BIAC4AKKAgwIABABGGUgYShZMA8=&rs=AOn4CLAayw7UOOMcLGnZ62RK_G-hTRs-8g", "description": " *\n *TWO ACCUSED ARRESTED & 10 STOLEN MOTOR CYCLES AND 2 MOTOR CYCLE LOCK BREAKING INSTRUMENTS RECOVERED.*\n *10 CASES OF M.V. THEFT CASEWS WORKED OUT WITH RECOVERY.*\n\nThe Special Staff of South West District has done a commendable work by arresting two accused of interstate mewati gang of auto lifters namely (1) Rahul S/o Saddik R/o Vill- Kaban Ka Bas, PS Khoh, Deeg, Distt- Bharat Pur, Rajasthan, Age 35 yrs & (2) Rashid S/o Taayib Hussain R/o Vill- Kaban Ka Bas, PS Khoh, Deeg, Distt- Bharat Pur, Rajasthan, Age 23 years. With their arrest, 10 stolen motor cycles and 2 motor cycle lock breaking instruments recovered.\n\n*INCIDENT, TEAM & ARREST:*\nKeeping in view the directions of senior officers and recent incidents of two wheelers theft, a dedicated team of Special Staff was tasked upon and CCTV footage of each incident were being checked and traps were continuously laid at various such hot spots in South West District. Besides, the team roped in various secret informers in this regard. The pain staking efforts of the team bore the result, when on 27.11.2022, secret information regarding two habitual Mewati Gang auto lifters was received at office of Special Staff and a team of Special Staff consisting of SI Manish Yadav, ASI Krishan Kumar, HC Shyam singh, HC Raju & HC Sandeep was formed under the leadership of Insp. Sanjay Kumar, I/C Special Staff and overall supervision of Sh. Devender Kumar Singh, ACP/Ops. to bust the gang. The team collected intelligence on the basis of modus operandi adopted by the gang and time chosen to commit crime and a trap was laid near Health center, Palam, Delhi. The raiding team acted swiftly and nabbed two members of Mewati auto lifters gang namely Rahul S/o Saddik, R/o Vill- Kaban Ka Bas, PS Khoh, Deeg, Distt- Bharat Pur, Rajasthan, Age 35 yrs & Rashid S/o Taayib Hussain, R/o Vill- Kaban Ka Bas, PS Khoh, Deeg, Distt- Bharat Pur, Rajasthan, Age 23 years, who came on a Hero Honda Splendor black colour motorcycle which was found stolen from PS Sagarpur, Delhi. Further on their instance, 9 more stolen motorcycles were also recovered from different areas of Delhi. Accordingly accused persons were arrested. \n\n        From their interrogation, it was revealed that accused Rahul and Rashid are drug addicts and habitual criminals. They have been arrested several times in Delhi, Rajasthan and Haryana. In the evening time, they used to conduct reconnaissance in different areas of Delhi NCR to identify soft targets and after identifying the area, they used to steal motorcycles from various parts of Delhi NCR and sell stolen motorcycles in Bharatpur, Rajasthan. So far, 10 cases of M.V Theft of Delhi have been worked out.\n\n*ACCUSED PERSONS DETAILS:*\n\n1. Rahul S/o Saddik R/o Vill- Kaban Ka Bas, PS Khoh, Deeg, Distt- Bharat Pur, \n    Rajasthan, Age 35 yrs is previously involved in 03 cases of theft.\n\n    (a) FIR no. 42/2010, u/s 379/411 IPC, PS Dabri, Dwarka, Delhi\n    (b) FIR no. 43/2010, u/s 379/411 IPC, PS Dabri, Dwarka, Delhi\n    (c) FIR no. 580/2004, u/s 411/34 IPC, PS Dwarka Sec23, Delhi\n\n2. Rashid S/o Taayib Hussain R/o Vill- Kaban Ka Bas, PS Khoh, Deeg, Distt- Bharat  \n    Pur, Rajasthan, Age 23 years is previously involved in 12 cases of theft. He is a  \n    habitual criminal and has been declared Proclaimed Offender by the court in   \n    FIR no. 157/2019, u/s 380/547 IPC, PS Palam, Delhi on 21.11.2022.\n\n1) FIR no. 10620/2020, u/s 379 IPC, PS South Campus, South West, Delhi\n2) FIR no. 10486/2020, u/s 379 IPC, PS South Campus, South West, Delhi\n3) FIR no. 025438/2018, u/s 379/411/482/34 IPC, PS Ghazipur, Delhi\n4) FIR no. 157/2019, u/s 380/547 IPC, PS Palam, Delhi\n5) FIR no. 006084/2020, u/s 379 IPC, PS Vasant Kunj North, South West, Delhi\n6) FIR no. 004391/2020, u/s 379 IPC, PS Vasant Kunj North, South West, Delhi\n7) FIR no. 490/2020, u/s 25 Arms Act & 411 IPC, PS Vasant Kunj South, South   West, Delhi\n8) FIR no. 0015429/2020, u/s 379 IPC, \n\n     *(MANOJ C.), IPS*\n     DY. COMMISSIONER OF POLICE\n     SOUTH WEST DISTT: NEW DELHI", "channel_id": "UCxuXzuDdRva6p_HaWYJY8RA", "channel_url": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCx